{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793773739,"nonce":"oA6JoBZG1eOw2N4xBIRZnEQoVYs=","title":"A runtime parameter inside an .evolves() formula is not supplied to the state readout","message":"A `jno.np.parameter` read in a state update, e.g. an initial history `H.evolves(maximum(H.i(-1), maximum(psi, H0(a))))` with the notch length `a` a parameter, fails at the first march step with KeyError \"Runtime parameter 'a' not supplied to the kernel. Ensure it was registered in runtime_parameter_tags and packed into InternalVars.volume_vars.\" The same parameter in a weak-form term works (`fem.solve(a=...)`).\n\nReproduction: a load-path march with `a = jno.np.parameter((1,), name='a')` used only inside an `.evolves(...)` formula, solved with `fem.solve(a=np.array([0.5]))`.\n\nExpected: the readout sees the runtime parameters the residual sees.","files":null}]}